{
  "dom_id": "step-q275826",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "For a discrete random variable $Y,$ the probability mass function $f(y)$ and the cumulative distribution function $F(y)$ are shown in the table below. Fill in the blanks.\n\n| $y$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(y)$ | $0.10$ | $0.25$ | $0.30$ | $0.20$ | $0.15$ |\n| $F(y)$ | $0.10$ | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} | $1$ |",
  "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $Y$ is a function $F(y)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(y)=P(Y\\le y).\n$$\n\nComputing $F(2),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(2) & =P(Y\\le 2) \\\\  & =P(Y\\in {1,2}) \\\\  & =f(1)+f(2) \\\\  & =0.10+0.25 \\\\  & =0.35.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $F(3),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(3) & =P(Y\\le 3) \\\\  & =P(Y\\in {1,2,3}) \\\\  & =f(1)+f(2)+f(3) \\\\  & =0.10+0.25+0.30 \\\\  & =0.65.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $F(4),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(4) & =P(Y\\le 4) \\\\  & =P(Y\\in {1,2,3,4}) \\\\  & =f(1)+f(2)+f(3)+f(4) \\\\  & =0.10+0.25+0.30+0.20 \\\\  & =0.85.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
